messages.content:
The TPM has reviewed your architecture guardrails for initiative "init-salescoach-mvp" and requested revision.

The TPM flagged the following concerns:

1. {
  "assessment": {
    "1_do_guardrails_address_requirements": {
      "functional": {
        "status": "partial",
        "mappedAcceptanceCriteria": [
          {
            "acId": "AC-05",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "AssemblyAI v3 streaming API interface exists (supports turn-level formatting and ForceEndpoint), aligning with real-time transcription requirements."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-10",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Cerebras and OpenAI interfaces both exist, which can support provider failover at the integration layer, but the failover orchestration behavior itself is not described in the guardrail summary."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-01",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Cerebras/OpenAI interfaces exist to enable LLM-powered Q1-Q3 intake/extraction, but orchestration, stop conditions, and field-filling loop are not described."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-02",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "SPICED+MEDDPICC guidebook data and precall questions schema interfaces exist, aligning with framework selection + missing-field question packs."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-07",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "LLM interfaces exist to generate post-call deliverables; no guardrails described for timing (<10s) or queueing/parallelization strategy."
          }
        ],
        "missingFunctionalPiecesNotInGuardrailsSummary": [
          "EventBus-only handler communication (AC-12) is not evidenced in the guardrails summary.",
          "Fire-once completion gating per callId (AC-03) is not evidenced.",
          "WebSocket reconnect behavior with max attempts/3s delay without losing call state (AC-09) is not evidenced.",
          "Confidence tagging for extracted data (AC-08) is not evidenced (no data contract / schema described).",
          "Coaching cue trigger detection, throttling policy, and sub-500ms on-screen cue ren

Please revise the guardrails to address the feedback. Return the complete revised guardrails as a JSON block:
```json
{ "version": "1.0", "interfaces": [...], "dataContracts": [...], "scalability": {...}, "securityBaseline": {...}, "adrs": [...], "metadata": {...} }
```
Make sure the JSON is valid and complete.

{
  "version": "1.0",
  "interfaces": [
    {
      "name": "WebSocket: live-call channel",
      "type": "api",
      "description": "Client<->backend WebSocket for streaming diarized transcript updates and coaching cues to the Angular UI; supports reconnect with call-state restoration.",
      "contract": "AC-05/AC-06/AC-09/AC-11: Messages sent over WebSocket MUST include callId and conform to transcriptTurn/coachingCue payload shapes defined in dataContracts. Client reconnect policy: max 5 attempts, 3s delay. On reconnect, server MUST restore state for the same callId from websocketCallStateSnapshot in MongoDB so call progression and latest transcript/cue sequence markers continue without loss."
    },
    {
      "name": "EventBus: backend internal pub/sub",
      "type": "event",
      "description": "Sole mechanism for backend module-to-module communication (no direct handler calls).",
      "contract": "AC-12: No direct handler-to-handler calls. All backend internal communication MUST flow through EventBus pub/sub. Stage progression and stage completion event publications MUST also be performed via EventBus."
    },
    {
      "name": "AssemblyAI v3 Streaming adapter",
      "type": "api",
      "description": "Streams audio to AssemblyAI and converts turn-level diarized results into internal transcriptTurn updates for WebSocket.",
      "contract": "AC-05/AC-12: Use AssemblyAI v3 streaming with format_turns=true and ForceEndpoint support (dependency). Adapter MUST produce diarized transcriptTurn updates (speaker rep vs prospect) and publish them via EventBus to WebSocket within the sub-500ms latency target for transcript display."
    },
    {
      "name": "LLM Provider Router (Cerebras primary, OpenAI fallback)",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Unifies structured outputs for PCRC-LLM Handler and performs transparent failover.",
      "contract": "AC-10: On Cerebras provider failure/degradation, router MUST transparently switch to OpenAI while preserving the unified structured output schema consumed by PCRC-LLM Handler and downstream renderers. Constraint: LLM model names MUST NOT be hardcoded; use CEREBRAS_DEFAULT_MODEL and OPENAI_DEFAULT_MODEL."
    },
    {
      "name": "PCRC-LLM Handler orchestrator",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Sole orchestrator for pre-call stages and related generation flows.",
      "contract": "AC-03/AC-01/AC-02/AC-04/AC-07: PCRC-LLM Handler MUST be the sole orchestrator for all pre-call stages (Constraint). It MUST execute CR1-CR5, Persona P1-P5, and Demographics D1-D5 sequentially. Each stage MUST be gated by a fire-once completion event exactly once per callId (enforced via Set<string> guards, constraint). It MUST generate callPlan (AC-04) and postCallDeliverables within 10 seconds of call end (AC-07)."
    },
    {
      "name": "GuidebookStore (SPICED+MEDDPICC loader)",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Loads SPICED/MEDDPICC JSON at startup and serves question packs for missing fields.",
      "contract": "AC-02: Framework selection returns SPICED (primary) + MEDDPICC (secondary) and proceeds to guidebook-derived question packs for missing fields. GuidebookStore MUST be populated at startup from provided JSON dependencies."
    },
    {
      "name": "PrecallQuestionSchema library",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Loads and validates precall-questions-schema.json to define Q1-Q3, required fields, and extraction rules.",
      "contract": "AC-01/AC-08: Must define the required fields and extraction rules for Q1-Q3 super-clarifying questions. Extraction outputs MUST include confidence tags (confirmed/inferred/assumed) for all extracted data."
    },
    {
      "name": "MongoDB CallState repository",
      "type": "database",
      "description": "Persists call sessions, state snapshot for reconnect, and generated artifacts (callPlan, postCallDeliverables).",
      "contract": "AC-09/AC-04/AC-07: Repository MUST persist websocketCallStateSnapshot keyed by callId to support reconnect state restoration without losing call state. Repository MUST store callPlan and postCallDeliverables with required fields."
    }
  ],
  "dataContracts": [
    {
      "entity": "ExtractedFieldValue",
      "storage": "MongoDB and/or EventBus payloads (implementation choice) under callSession scope",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-08: { fieldKey: string, value: any, confidenceTag: 'confirmed'|'inferred'|'assumed', extractedAtIso?: string }. All extracted data MUST carry confidenceTag."
    },
    {
      "entity": "PrecallIntakeResult",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-01/AC-08: { callId, requiredFieldsStatus: { [fieldKey: string]: 'complete'|'missing' }, extractedFields: ExtractedFieldValue[], completedAtIso }. Stop condition is all required fields complete."
    },
    {
      "entity": "StageCompletionEvent",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus (optionally mirrored for debug)",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-03/AC-12/constraint: { eventType: 'stageCompleted', callId, stageGroup: 'CR'|'Persona'|'Demographics', stageId: 'CR1'..'CR5'|'P1'..'P5'|'D1'..'D5', completedAtIso, attemptSequence: number }. Exactly-once per callId is enforced via per-call Set<string> guards before publishing."
    },
    {
      "entity": "FrameworkSelectionResult",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-02: { callId, primaryFramework: 'SPICED', secondaryFramework: 'MEDDPICC', missingFieldQuestionPackRefs: string[], selectedAtIso }."
    },
    {
      "entity": "callPlan",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-04: { callId, objective: string, priorities: string[3], risks: string[2], targetNextStep: string, unknowns: string[] }."
    },
    {
      "entity": "transcriptTurn",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus -> WebSocket; optional persistence under callSession",
      "ownership": "AssemblyAI adapter + WebSocket publisher",
      "notes": "AC-05: { callId, turnSequence: number, speaker: 'rep'|'prospect', text: string, startedAtIso?: string, endedAtIso?: string }. Delivered such that UI can render at sub-500ms latency."
    },
    {
      "entity": "coachingCue",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus -> WebSocket; optional persistence under callSession",
      "ownership": "Coaching cue service (trigger detection + policy) or PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-06: { callId, cueSequence: number, cueText: string, triggerType: string, triggeredAtIso: string, uiDeadlineMs: number, suppressionApplied: boolean, suppressionReason?: string }. Throttling/suppression policy: max 1 cue per 30 seconds (contract says 30-45s; enforce <=30s for verifiability) and suppress cues when transcription confidence drops."
    },
    {
      "entity": "websocketCallStateSnapshot",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "backend (WebSocket state service)",
      "notes": "AC-09: { callId, currentStage: 'CR'|'Persona'|'Demographics'|'PostCall' with optional current stageId, completedStageIds: string[], lastTranscriptTurnSequence?: number, lastCueSequence?: number, frameworkSelectionPresent: boolean, updatedAtIso }. Used on reconnect to resume without losing call state."
    },
    {
      "entity": "postCallDeliverables",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-07: generated within 10 seconds of call end. { callId, generatedAtIso, summary: string, scorecard: { categories: string[8] }, strength: string, improvementArea: string, practiceRecommendation: string }."
    }
  ],
  "scalability": {
    "expectedLoad": "Not specified in contract. Assumed single-rep private usage with live WebSocket streaming. Dominant loads: AssemblyAI streaming turn events and UI rendering updates (transcriptTurn + coachingCue), plus occasional LLM calls for cues, plans, and post-call deliverables (AC-05/AC-06/AC-07/AC-09/AC-11).",
    "bottlenecks": [
      "Latency path AssemblyAI turn arrival -> transcriptTurn publish -> WebSocket send -> UI render (AC-05).",
      "Cue generation and cue emission timing budget around trigger detection -> cue policy -> WebSocket -> UI render (AC-06).",
      "EventBus fan-out and UI update churn potentially causing jank (AC-11).",
      "WebSocket reconnect rehydration time if websocketCallStateSnapshot retrieval is slow (AC-09).",
      "LLM provider failover can add tail latency if failover is not handled at adapter/router level (AC-10)."
    ],
    "mitigations": [
      "Minimize adapter processing: transform AssemblyAI turn events directly into transcriptTurn and publish immediately (AC-05, AC-12).",
      "Enforce cue throttling/suppression server-side before expensive operations; only emit coachingCue when policy allows; include uiDeadlineMs for UI scheduling (AC-06).",
      "Frontend must use OnPush and explicitly markForCheck() on async transcript/cue updates to avoid jank (AC-11).",
      "Persist websocketCallStateSnapshot and retrieve by callId with indices; ensure reconnect rehydration is bounded (AC-09).",
      "Implement LLM Provider Router failover to preserve unified schema and avoid downstream parsing delays (AC-10)."
    ]
  },
  "securityBaseline": {
    "authMethod": "TBD/assumed: TPM contract does not specify auth. For production readiness, implement at least a single-user session gate (assumed derived from single-rep private tool + sensitivity of transcripts/cues) to protect WebSocket call streams and callId-based snapshot access (AC-09 risk).",
    "dataClassification": "Assumed sensitive: live call transcripts with diarization, extracted fields with confidence tags, coaching cues, call plans, and post-call deliverables.",
    "threatVectors": [
      "Unauthorized access to WebSocket stream allowing transcript/coaching leakage (AC-09).",
      "Call state leakage/cross-call bleed if callId scoping is incorrect (AC-09) and exact-once stage completion guards are mis-keyed (AC-03).",
      "Duplicate stage completion events due to retries/reconnect leading to inconsistent UI/stage progression (AC-03).",
      "LLM prompt injection via transcript content producing incorrect coaching cues/extractions (AC-01/AC-06).",
      "Malformed/unexpected structured output during provider failover causing UI parsing failures and timing misses (AC-10)."
    ],
    "mitigations": [
      "Enforce callId scoping and authorization checks on every WebSocket message and every websocketCallStateSnapshot retrieval (AC-09; assumed).",
      "Enforce exact-once stage completion via per-call Set<string> guard keyed by callId+stageId prior to publishing StageCompletionEvent (AC-03).",
      "Validate payloads against dataContract shapes before emitting to WebSocket/UI (supports AC-06/AC-08/AC-04/AC-07).",
      "Use unified structured output schema preserved across failover in LLM Provider Router (AC-10).",
      "Keep cue throttling/suppression server-side regardless of client behavior (AC-06)."
    ]
  },
  "adrs": [
    {
      "id": "ADR-001",
      "title": "EventBus-only internal communication (AC-12)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-12: All event-driven communication flows through EventBus — no direct handler-to-handler calls. Constraint: handler communication must flow through EventBus pub/sub system.",
      "decision": "Implement a single backend EventBus pub/sub layer and require all internal module interactions (including stage progression updates) to use publish/subscribe; prohibit direct handler-to-handler calls via code review and/or lint rule.",
      "consequences": "Improves decoupling and enforces the contractual architectural constraint; debugging relies on event logs."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-002",
      "title": "PCRC-LLM Handler is the sole pre-call orchestrator with exact-once stage completion (AC-03)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-03: Call Reasoning (CR1-CR5), Persona (P1-P5), and Demographics (D1-D5) stages complete sequentially, each gated by a fire-once completion event. Constraint: PCRC-LLM Handler is the sole orchestrator for all pre-call stages; old individual handlers disabled. Constraint: stage completion events must fire exactly once per callId enforced via Set<string> guards.",
      "decision": "Route all pre-call stage logic through PCRC-LLM Handler. Maintain a per-call Set<string> of emitted stageIds and publish StageCompletionEvent to EventBus only once per callId+stageId; enforce sequential progression in the orchestrator.",
      "consequences": "Prevents duplicate stage emissions and race conditions across retries/reconnects; centralizes orchestration logic."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-003",
      "title": "Confidence-tagged extraction loop with schema-driven stop conditions (AC-01, AC-08)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-01: Pre-call conversational intake completes Q1-Q3 super-clarifying questions with LLM-driven extraction until all required fields are filled. AC-08: All extracted data carries confidence tags (confirmed, inferred, assumed). Dependency: precall-questions-schema.json defines extraction rules and required fields.",
      "decision": "Derive required fields and extraction rules from precall-questions-schema.json. Represent outputs as ExtractedFieldValue {value, confidenceTag} and iterate until requiredFieldsStatus is complete; never allow extracted outputs without confidenceTag.",
      "consequences": "Ensures AC-08 verifiability and provides deterministic intake termination based on schema-defined required fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-004",
      "title": "Transparent LLM failover via provider router preserving unified structured outputs (AC-10)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-10: LLM provider failover switches between Cerebras and OpenAI transparently on provider failure. Constraint: LLM model names must never be hardcoded; use environment-configured defaults CEREBRAS_DEFAULT_MODEL and OPENAI_DEFAULT_MODEL.",
      "decision": "Implement an LLM Provider Router used by PCRC-LLM Handler. Attempt Cerebras first; on provider failure/degraded response switch to OpenAI while keeping the same unified structured output schema expected by the rest of the system.",
      "consequences": "Meets AC-10 and reduces downstream failures during provider changes/failures."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-005",
      "title": "AssemblyAI streaming diarized transcript rendering at sub-500ms latency (AC-05)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-05: Live transcription displays with speaker diarization at sub-500ms latency via AssemblyAI streaming. Dependency: AssemblyAI v3 streaming with format_turns=true and ForceEndpoint support.",
      "decision": "Enable AssemblyAI streaming with format_turns=true and ForceEndpoint support. Convert turn events directly into transcriptTurn payloads and publish via EventBus to WebSocket with minimal transformation overhead to support the sub-500ms render target.",
      "consequences": "Supports diarization and minimizes latency overhead; actual achieved latency depends on network and UI rendering."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-006",
      "title": "Coaching cue policy: 500ms trigger-to-render, throttling, and suppression (AC-06)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-06: Coaching cues appear on-screen within 500ms of trigger detection, throttled to max 1 per 30 seconds. Constraint: cues must be non-intrusive max 1 per 30-45 seconds and suppressible when transcription confidence drops.",
      "decision": "Implement server-side cue policy service that enforces: (1) max 1 cue per 30 seconds, (2) suppression when transcription confidence drops, (3) attaches timing fields (triggeredAtIso/uiDeadlineMs) so UI can schedule rendering to meet 500ms. Publish coachingCue only when policy allows.",
      "consequences": "Prevents cue spam and aligns cue delivery behavior with AC-06 verifiability."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-007",
      "title": "WebSocket reconnect state restoration without losing call state (AC-09)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-09: WebSocket reconnects automatically (max 5 attempts, 3s delay) without losing call state. Constraint: exact-once stage completion per callId enforced via Set<string> guards (AC-03).",
      "decision": "Persist websocketCallStateSnapshot keyed by callId. On reconnect, client sends callId; server rehydrates stage completion markers and latest transcript/cue sequence markers from the snapshot and continues streaming updates without re-triggering completed stages.",
      "consequences": "Meets AC-09 and preserves correctness of sequential stage progression across transient network drops."
    },
    {
      "id": "ADR-008",
      "title": "Post-call deliverables timing budget (<10s) and structured schema (AC-07)",
      "status": "accepted",
      "context": "AC-07: Post-call summary, scorecard, and lessons are generated within 10 seconds of call end.",
      "decision": "Trigger postCallDeliverables generation on call end and enforce an end-to-end 10-second budget for producing the structured output (summary, scorecard categories size 8, strength, improvementArea, practiceRecommendation).",
      "consequences": "Meets end-to-end responsiveness requirement for MVP review loop."
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "derivedFrom": "tpm-contract.json",
    "confidenceMap": {
      "interfaces": "confirmed",
      "dataContracts": "inferred",
      "scalability": "assumed",
      "securityBaseline": "assumed",
      "adrs": "confirmed"
    },
    "gaps": [
      "Auth method is not specified in the TPM contract; securityBaseline.authMethod remains assumed/TBD for verification. This is a readiness gap for production hardening.",
      "Exact AssemblyAI turn event fields and transcription confidence representation are not specified; cue suppression relies on transcription confidence drops but the confidence signal format is not defined in contract.",
      "Trigger detection algorithm inputs/outputs are not specified; only cue throttling/suppression and timing are defined."
    ]
  }
}

{
  "version": "1.0",
  "interfaces": [
    {
      "name": "WebSocket: live-call channel",
      "type": "api",
      "description": "Client<->backend WebSocket for streaming diarized transcript turns and coaching cues; supports reconnect to resume without losing call state.",
      "contract": "AC-05/AC-06/AC-09/AC-11: All WebSocket payloads include callId. Client reconnect behavior: max 5 attempts, 3s delay. On reconnect, backend MUST rehydrate call progress and resume streaming from state persisted under websocketCallStateSnapshot keyed by callId in MongoDB, preserving latest transcriptTurn and coachingCue sequence markers so UI does not regress or lose state."
    },
    {
      "name": "EventBus: backend internal pub/sub",
      "type": "event",
      "description": "Event-only internal communication mechanism; forbids direct handler-to-handler calls.",
      "contract": "AC-12: No direct handler-to-handler calls. All backend module interactions (including stage progression, transcript publish, cue publish, and call-end triggering) MUST use EventBus publish/subscribe."
    },
    {
      "name": "AssemblyAI v3 Streaming adapter",
      "type": "api",
      "description": "Adapter consuming AssemblyAI v3 streaming with diarization/turn formatting and emitting transcriptTurn updates.",
      "contract": "AC-05: Use AssemblyAI v3 streaming with format_turns=true and ForceEndpoint support. Adapter MUST emit diarized transcriptTurn events (speaker rep vs prospect). End-to-end from adapter to UI render must be engineered for sub-500ms; contract check is via client-side instrumentation of render timestamp minus adapter publish timestamp."
    },
    {
      "name": "LLM Provider Router (Cerebras primary -> OpenAI fallback)",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Unified structured-output failover router used by PCRC-LLM Handler.",
      "contract": "AC-10: Router transparently switches Cerebras->OpenAI on provider failure/degradation. The structured output schema MUST remain identical so downstream processors (extraction, cue trigger decisions, call plan, post-call deliverables) do not change across providers. Constraint: model names are environment-configured only (CEREBRAS_DEFAULT_MODEL, OPENAI_DEFAULT_MODEL)."
    },
    {
      "name": "PCRC-LLM Handler orchestrator",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Sole orchestrator for pre-call conversational intake and sequential stages; triggers call plan generation and post-call deliverables.",
      "contract": "AC-01/AC-02/AC-03/AC-04/AC-07: PCRC-LLM Handler is the sole orchestrator for all pre-call stages; old handlers remain disabled (constraint). It MUST execute sequential stage groups CR1-CR5 -> Persona P1-P5 -> Demographics D1-D5. Each stage completion MUST be gated by exactly-once completion event per callId enforced via Set<string> guards. It MUST generate callPlan with required fields (AC-04) and post-call deliverables within 10 seconds of call end (AC-07)."
    },
    {
      "name": "GuidebookStore (SPICED+MEDDPICC JSON loader)",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "In-memory question packs store loaded at startup.",
      "contract": "AC-02: After framework selection returns SPICED (primary) + MEDDPICC (secondary), PCRC-LLM Handler requests guidebook-derived question packs for missing fields from GuidebookStore."
    },
    {
      "name": "PrecallQuestionSchema library",
      "type": "shared-lib",
      "description": "Schema loader defining Q1-Q3 questions, required fields, and extraction rules.",
      "contract": "AC-01/AC-08: Schema defines required fields and extraction rules for Q1-Q3 intake. All extraction results MUST include confidenceTag ∈ {confirmed,inferred,assumed} for every extracted field (AC-08)."
    },
    {
      "name": "MongoDB CallState + Snapshots repository",
      "type": "database",
      "description": "Persists call sessions, stage completion markers, sequence markers, call plan, post-call deliverables, and reconnect snapshots.",
      "contract": "AC-09: repository MUST persist websocketCallStateSnapshot keyed by callId. It MUST be sufficient to rehydrate stage progression and latest transcriptTurn/coachingCue sequence markers on WebSocket reconnect without losing call state."
    }
  ],
  "dataContracts": [
    {
      "entity": "ExtractedFieldValue",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession and/or EventBus payloads within call scope",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-08 (verifiable): { fieldKey: string, value: any, confidenceTag: 'confirmed'|'inferred'|'assumed', updatedAtIso?: string }. Every extracted field MUST include confidenceTag."
    },
    {
      "entity": "PrecallIntakeResult",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-01/AC-08: { callId, requiredFieldsStatus: { [fieldKey: string]: 'complete'|'missing' }, extractedFields: ExtractedFieldValue[], intakeCompletedAtIso?: string }."
    },
    {
      "entity": "StageCompletionEvent",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus (optionally mirrored to MongoDB for debugging)",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-03/AC-12 (behavioral + semantic): { eventType: 'stageCompleted', callId, stageGroup: 'CR'|'Persona'|'Demographics', stageId: 'CR1'..'CR5'|'P1'..'P5'|'D1'..'D5', completedAtIso, attemptSequence: number }. Exactly-once: for each callId+stageId, the system emits at most once (enforced by Set<string> guard)."
    },
    {
      "entity": "FrameworkSelectionResult",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-02: { callId, primaryFramework:'SPICED', secondaryFramework:'MEDDPICC', missingFieldQuestionPackRefs: string[], selectedAtIso }."
    },
    {
      "entity": "CallPlan",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-04: { callId, objective: string, priorities: string[3], risks: string[2], targetNextStep: string, unknowns: string[] }."
    },
    {
      "entity": "transcriptTurn",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus -> WebSocket; optional persistence",
      "ownership": "AssemblyAI adapter",
      "notes": "AC-05: { callId, turnSequence: number, speaker: 'rep'|'prospect', text: string, startedAtIso?: string, endedAtIso?: string, adapterPublishedAtMs: number }. The adapterPublishedAtMs enables measurement of adapter-to-UI render timing."
    },
    {
      "entity": "coachingCue",
      "storage": "transient via EventBus -> WebSocket; optional persistence",
      "ownership": "Cue policy service and PCRC-LLM Handler trigger logic",
      "notes": "AC-06: { callId, cueSequence: number, cueText: string, triggerType: string, triggeredAtIso: string, uiDeadlineMs: number, throttlingWindowMs: number, suppressionApplied: boolean, suppressionReason?: string }. Throttle/suppression semantics are enforced server-side: max 1 cue per 30 seconds and suppression when transcription confidence drops."
    },
    {
      "entity": "websocketCallStateSnapshot",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "MongoDB CallState repository",
      "notes": "AC-09: { callId, currentStage: { stageGroup: 'CR'|'Persona'|'Demographics'|'PostCall', stageId?: string }, completedStageIds: string[], lastTranscriptTurnSequence?: number, lastCueSequence?: number, frameworkSelectionPresent: boolean, updatedAtIso: string }. Used to rehydrate on reconnect without losing call state."
    },
    {
      "entity": "PostCallDeliverables",
      "storage": "MongoDB under callSession",
      "ownership": "PCRC-LLM Handler",
      "notes": "AC-07: { callId, generatedAtIso, summary: string, scorecard: { categories: string[8] }, strength: string, improvementArea: string, practiceRecommendation: string }."
    }
  ],
  "scalability": {
    "expectedLoad": "Contract implies single-rep private tool. Live call load scales with (a) AssemblyAI streaming turn frequency and (b) coaching cue frequency throttled to max 1 cue per 30 seconds (AC-06). LLM calls occur during pre-call intake, cue trigger generation, and post-call deliverables (AC-01/AC-06/AC-07).",
    "bottlenecks": [
      "Latency-critical path: AssemblyAI turn arrival -> transcriptTurn publish -> WebSocket send -> UI render (AC-05).",
      "Latency-critical path: trigger detection -> cue policy decision -> coachingCue publish -> UI render (AC-06).",
      "UI performance risk under concurrent updates if OnPush/markForCheck is not correctly used (AC-11).",
      "Reliability risk: WebSocket reconnect rehydration must be correct and fast using websocketCallStateSnapshot (AC-09).",
      "Provider failover tail latency and schema drift risk during transparent switching (AC-10)."
